  "subtitle": "[ASSET: left | SheFainted | width=51%] This month's VMA goes to [LINK:1963:JIM_99_thor0|JIM #99], where we find Jane Foster, having just witnessed Don Blake getting thrown out of an upper-story window...\n[BR]\n[BR] The caption reads:\n[BR] [SPAN: severity=warning; fontsize=larger; fonttype=bold; text=And then, because she <i>is</i> a female...]\n[BR]\n[BR] Mr. Hyde says, \"She <b><i>fainted</i></b>!\"\n[BR]\n[BR] [SPAN: fontsize=small; severity=info; fonttype=italic; text=(OMG!)]",
  "review_text": "Not a stellar month for Marvel, with 8 graded stories spread out over 6 books (both Amazing Spider-Man and Strange Tales had two), averaging only a middling 4.08, which is just barely at \"reader\" level.&nbsp; The <i>Strange Tales</i> #116, in particular, dragged the average down by over half a point (as far as I'm concerned, Doctor Strange is still a no-show) - let's face it - Marvel did little this month to provide quality to its readers above just an average <i>Meh</i> rating.\n\nOn the positive side were the crossovers (though Spider-Man crashing Johnny's party was ghastly and should never have been done) and the appearance by the Watcher.&nbsp; And the main story from ASM was solid, as was the FF issue, but they were only around mid-grade, so nothing earth-shattering.\n\nHaving both Jan and the Watcher serve as story-tellers in this month's issues is interesting, but it's mostly dressing around the back-up tales in the various anthology-style books.\n\n\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** SUMMARY_BEGIN ***\n*** THIS MONTH ***8 graded stories over 6 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 4.58 grade character issue   weight 6.5   asm       ASM #8  0.75 6.0   ff        FF #22  1.00 4.5   iron      TOS #49 0.75 4.0   thor      JIM #99 0.50 3.5   giant     TTA #51 0.50 3.0   asm       ASM #8  0.25 2.0   strange   ST #116 0.33 1.5   torch     ST #116 0.504.40*** LAST MONTH ***9 graded stories over 8 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 6.58 grade character issue   weight 6.0   asm       ASM #7  1.00 5.5   strange   ST #115 0.33 5.0   thor      JIM #98 0.50 5.0   giant     TTA #50 0.50 5.0   torch     ST #115 0.50 5.0   iron      TOS #48 0.75 4.0   ff        FF #21  1.00 3.0   xmen      XMEN #2 1.00 1.5   aven      AVEN #2 1.004.19\n*** SUMMARY_END ***]",
  "letters_page": "[HANG0] * Introduction of Mr. Hyde\n[HANG0] * Peter Parker punching Flash Thompson in the boxing ring\n[HANG0] * Sue Storm finally getting some offensive powers\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** INTRODUCTION_BEGIN ***\nMister Hyde | villain | Milestone: (first), (origin)\nNotes | first | villain | Living Brain\n*** INTRODUCTION_END ***]\n\n<b>Roundup:</b>\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_BEGIN ***]\n[HANG0] * FIXME -- write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME -- write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME -- write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME -- write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME -- write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME -- write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME -- write something\n[HANG0] * FIXME -- write something\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_END ***]",
